WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.660
As promised, the Terminator franchise came
back... but it didn't arrive to the kind of

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.140
financial success that studio Paramount Pictures
was hoping for.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.440
Terminator: Dark Fate, the sixth entry into
the Terminator film series that acts as a

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:20.790
direct sequel to 1984's Terminator and 1991's
Terminator: Judgment Day, opened in theaters

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.140
on Friday, November 1 to dismal box office
returns.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:30.300
Despite having James Cameron back on board
as a producer, Deadpool director Tim Miller

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.460
behind the helm, Arnold Schwarzenegger and
Linda Hamilton in their respective roles as

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:39.270
the T-800 Terminator and the gun-toting badass
Sarah Connor, and a host of intriguing new

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.660
characters in the mix, Dark Fate sadly lived
up to its name facing a dark fate by earning

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:51.020
just $29 million domestically and $94.6 million
internationally over its opening weekend.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.740
That's not good for a franchise trying so
desperately to redeem itself.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.720
"If something goes wrong, this could be our
last chance — so MOVE!"

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:05.980
With a total debut pull of $123.6 million,
Terminator: Dark Fate hasn't come close to

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:11.650
recouping its reported production budget of
$185 million, which doesn't include the cost

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.220
of marketing and distribution.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:17.520
According to The Hollywood Reporter, this
means that Dark Fate could end up costing

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:23.460
Paramount Pictures, Skydance Media, and the
now-shuttered 20th Century Fox more than $120

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.160
million.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:30.270
Each company is said to have financed 30 percent
of the film's budget, which works out to about

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.100
$55.5 million a pop.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:37.140
The remaining 10 percent of Dark Fate's production
budget is on the line at the Chinese conglomerate

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.480
Tencent Holdings.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:46.220
THR details the worst-case scenario for Terminator:
Dark Fate as costing its financiers $130 million

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:50.260
in the event that the film loses its overseas
traction and winds up flopping.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.660
A source close to the outlet has indicated
that the better-case scenario is that Paramount,

00:01:54.660 --> 00:02:01.660
Skydance, Fox owner Disney, and Tencent may
end up eating only $110 million if Dark Fate,

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.000
quote, "does have strong legs offshore."

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.879
Still, Variety reports that Terminator: Dark
Fate is looking at a worldwide take-home of

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:14.290
only $180 million to $200 million dollars,
and that the film would need to earn around

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.380
$450 million total just to break even.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.160
It would be simple to say that Dark Fate tanked
at the box office because critics and fans

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.860
absolutely hated it and think it's a massive
piece of garbage, but that would be a lie.

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:31.359
It seems a big reason why Terminator: Dark
Fate tanked financially isn't because everyone

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.590
thinks the film is horrible.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.519
Rather, it appears that the films that preceded
Dark Fate the much-derided Terminator 3: Rise

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:44.010
of the Machines, Terminator Salvation, and
Terminator Genisys, all of which Dark Fate

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:49.180
actually ignores were so bad that people aren't
giving the new movie a chance.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:54.349
Fewer people heading out to theaters naturally
means less revenue, and it looks as though

00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:58.000
this is the situation in which Dark Fate is
currently stuck.

00:02:58.189 --> 00:03:03.340
For some fans, the fact that Terminator: Dark
Fate is being touted as a franchise-reviver

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.140
might instill in them a terrible sense of
déjà vu.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.980
After all, 2015's Terminator Genisys was also
marketed as a something of a breath of fresh

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.159
air to the struggling franchise, with Game
of Thrones' Emilia Clarke stepping into the

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.760
role of Sarah Connor, and wound up getting
ripped to shreds by everyone who saw it.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:24.980
There's a strong chance people are afraid
Dark Fate is just Genisys with different packaging

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.600
which really isn't accurate.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.600
"Never seen one like you before.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.220
Almost human."

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:31.760
"I am human.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Just enhanced."

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.580
"Which means I can rip your throat out if
you piss me off."

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.940
Rotten Tomatoes reviews for Terminator: Dark
Fate are fairly solid.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.200
The film sits at a respectable 70 percent
critical rating.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.460
It's consensus?

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:48.560
"Terminator: Dark Fate represents a significant
upgrade over its immediate predecessors, even

00:03:48.579 --> 00:03:52.639
if it lacks the thrilling firepower of the
franchise's best installments."

00:03:52.639 --> 00:03:57.469
Sure, some critics weren't super fond of the
flick, but others found it truly enjoyable

00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:02.159
like TheWrap's William Bibbiani, who said
of Dark Fate, quote, "This story actually

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.920
demands to be told, and it gets told with
precision and skill."

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.480
For their part, fans liked Dark Fate better
than critics did.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.349
The film's audience rating on Rotten Tomatoes
is clocking in at 84 percent as of the making

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:14.920
of this video.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:20.280
Overall, Terminator: Dark Fate may not be
a mind-blowing piece of cinema or a universal

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.980
crowd-pleaser, but it isn't avoid-at-all-costs
awful.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.420
It's a pretty good film with pretty good ratings.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.440
But regardless of what Dark Fate has going
for it Cameron returning as producer, Schwarzenegger

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.950
and Hamilton back in action, a new story to
tell, passable reviews it still floundered

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.080
at the box office.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:43.140
Unless Terminator: Dark Fate somehow does
the impossible and earns an unthinkable amount

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:46.780
of money in the very near future, things aren't
looking good for the franchise.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:51.560
What was intended to be a balm to help heal
the film series may have just made it even

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.760
sicker and possibly even pushed it to its
doom.

